   "claims": [
    "🙋 The gravel calculator initially assumes a default gravel density of 1680 kg/m³ or 105 lbs/ft³.",
    "Instantly, the calculator tells you that you require 0.75 m³ of gravel, which weighs 1.26 tonnes.",
    "The calculator immediately tells you the depth you can fill with gravel is 11.90476 cm (approximately 12 cm).",
    "Normally, we would like our gravel path to consist of 2 or 3 different layers of gravel.",
    "First, we need to divide the pea gravel path into four rectangles: 1, 2, 3, and 4.",
    "1 ton of gravel is equal to 0.714 cubic yards.",
    "To convert tons of gravel into yards, simply multiply tons by 0.714.",
    "For example, 2 tons of gravel is 2 × 0.714 = 1.428 cubic yards, 3 tons is equal to 3 × 0.714 = 2.142, and so on.",
    "A cubic yard of gravel can weigh between 2,400 lbs (1,089 kg) to 2,900 lbs (1,315 kg).",
    "Assuming you have a 10 ft long by 10 ft wide by 2\" high driveway, the amount of gravel will be 0.617 cubic yards or 0.794 tons."
   ],
